<title>UK: NIB sets 100 billion lire equity-linked bond.</title>
<headline>NIB sets 100 billion lire equity-linked bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Cariplo and Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NORDIC INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    100 BLN LIRE  COUPON     *ZERO     MATURITY    18.MAR.02</p>
<p> TYPE   MIB 30 LINKED ISS PRICE  101.50    PAY DATE    18.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 REC REOFF  99.875    LISTING     LONDON</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY   =</p>
<p> NOTES	*FOR YEAR ONE, IN YEAR TWO COUPON IS LINKED TO THE</p>
<p>		 MIB-30 INDEX AND THEREAFTER IS 9.0 PCT SUBJECT TO A</p>
<p>		 COUPON OPTION ON MARCH 1999 WHICH GIVES THE ISSUER</p>
<p>		 THE OPTION TO CONVERT FROM A FIXED RATE COUPON TO</p>
<p>		 SIX-MONTH LIBOR PLUS 25 BP.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
